From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:09:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] widl: Skip the empty arms of a union in a type library.

A union arm with no member, such as STGMEDIUM's [case(TYMED_NULL)],
has no type, and writing its variable description dereferenced it:
widl crashed building a type library from msinkaut.idl, whose
clipboard methods bring IDataObject and so STGMEDIUM into the library.
Such an arm has nothing to describe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/tools/widl/write_msft.c b/tools/widl/write_msft.c
index 6c63e2716b7..66f2e73c203 100644
--- a/tools/widl/write_msft.c
+++ b/tools/widl/write_msft.c
@@ -2285,7 +2285,11 @@ static void add_union_typeinfo(msft_typelib_t *typelib, type_t *tunion)
 
     if (type_union_get_cases(tunion))
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(cur, type_union_get_cases(tunion), var_t, entry)
+        {
+            /* an empty arm, such as STGMEDIUM's for TYMED_NULL, has no member to describe */
+            if (!cur->declspec.type) continue;
             add_var_desc(msft_typeinfo, idx++, cur);
+        }
 }
 
 static void add_typedef_typeinfo(msft_typelib_t *typelib, type_t *tdef)
